{"c":[{"id":"2f09076641c97656","sum":"B21: planRequest names a window by {pid,number,title} or windowId, never both (unread = unseenWindow); rebuild caret-screen after mutated swift tests; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; Return in a frontmost one-line field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09ccc8ad4b5ca18a","sum":"planRequest names its window by {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; unread = unseenWindow, neither = ScreenModel.userWindow (v2/host planError needs an unseenWindow sentence). swift test on mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen: rebuild before GUI evals.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-41933c0bb214864e","text":"planRequest names its window as window {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; an unread one is unseenWindow; neither means the frontmost app's last focused window (ScreenModel.userWindow). v2/host's planError switch needs an unseenWindow sentence (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-53ebaedecebf757b","text":"swift test on a mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from the restored source before any GUI eval runs those binaries (B21 caught it by timestamp).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f69cdfcee30c7eb9","sum":"B21: keys posted to an inactive app's pid skip AppKit key equivalents (posted Return never ran the default button, Space pressed a focused one); frontmost, Return in a single-line field presses the default button, which the reader does not report.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-ebf44f31f7890c91","text":"A key posted to a pid whose app is not active skips AppKit key equivalents: the fixture's default button never ran on posted Return or Enter (0 of 10), Space pressed a focused button 5 of 5. The reader places key presses from cached focus and default button (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9b3d66084a009c9f","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked on close; evals call helper.hostConnected); pause/stop/settings/disconnect revoke the act grant at once, Helper.authorize before each act; mutation runs use swift test --build-path /tmp, grep 'recorded an issue'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dc5a5754f076b1b1","sum":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks bind to it and are revoked when it closes; in-process evals must call helper.hostConnected(id). Pause, stop, settings and disconnect revoke the act grant at once; Helper.authorize is asked before each act.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccdfe7e5f11e70bf","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked when it closes; evals call helper.hostConnected). Mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps .build/debug clean; Swift Testing prints 'recorded an issue' for a failure, grep that.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
